export anchor AmberTerminalStyle:
    number: 290
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Amber terminal
    idea: A full-screen amber text-mode application of double-ruled panes with titles set into their borders, an inverse selection bar, a top status line and a bottom function key bar, glowing warmly on black.
    base: dark
    palette:
        black: #0c0700, the page, pane interiors and the style sheet
        amber: #ffb000, main text, double rules, the inverse bar and focus
        dim: #d39300, labels, line numbers, removed lines and the key bar captions
        rule: #8a5c00, single inner dividers, never text
        inverseInk: #0c0700, text on the amber inverse bar, pane titles and buttons
    type:
        One monospace stack, Fixedsys, Terminus, DejaVu Sans Mono, Lucida Console,
        ui-monospace, Consolas, at 14px on 1.5. Pane titles 14px at 700 caps tracked
        0.08em in inverse. The title 18px at 700. Function key bar 13px. Amber
        glyphs carry a 5px warm glow.
    layout:
        A full width text-mode screen. A one line inverse status bar shows
        Brightwork Code, the repository, Private and Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3.
        Below, a grid of panes with 3px double amber borders, each with its title
        set into the top border as an inverse tag. Row one has three panes, a 240px
        Repository pane listing the six tabs with Pull requests on the inverse
        selection bar and a pointer, a wide Pull request 214 pane with the title,
        Open, the merge sentence and a key and value table for reviewers, labels,
        assignees, milestone and linked issue, and a 300px Checks pane listing all
        twelve checks with a mark and a word and the failing row inverted. Row two
        has a Files pane with three rows of counts and a wide Diff pane with the
        hunk and the boxed comment. A function key bar runs along the bottom with
        keys as inverse numbers and captions, including F8 Merge shown locked and
        disabled. Below 1000px the panes stack in one column and the key bar wraps.
    spacing:
        A character grid. 8px horizontal and 4px vertical cell padding, 12px inside
        panes, 8px between panes.
    density: Dense. A full screen of text, every pane visible at once on a laptop.
    corners: Square everywhere.
    borders:
        3px double amber borders around panes, 1px rule dividers inside them, titles
        cut into the top border.
    shadows: No box shadows. Text has a 5px amber glow at 45 percent.
    icons:
        Line icons at 2px stroke in amber at 1em with square caps, always with the
        word. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing,
        triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge.
    focus: The inverse selection bar, amber fill with black text, plus a 2px amber outline offset 2px.
    tone:
        Utility program voice, short caps titles and terse captions, such as CHECKS
        11/12 and F8 Merge locked.
